# How to choose

The axis is NOT "is a message being sent?" - it is "is this COMMUNICATING with the user, or DOING something?". Ask in order:

1. **Is the node COMMUNICATIVE - its job is to deliver a heads-up, reminder, nudge, or question to the USER ({{ resource_user_data.first_name }}), surfaced in their UI?** Verbs like "Notify {{ resource_user_data.first_name }}...", "Remind {{ resource_user_data.first_name }}...", "Tell {{ resource_user_data.first_name }}...", "Ask {{ resource_user_data.first_name }}...", "Nudge/Prompt {{ resource_user_data.first_name }}..." are ALWAYS communicative - INCLUDING when the user is asked to DO something themselves ("Ask {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} to submit his timesheets", "Nudge {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} to take a break"). Nothing is composed and dispatched through a channel - it is a UI ping the user reads (or answers) directly. The worker CANNOT do these for the user; only {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} can.
   -> `create_dayflow_ticket`. Any "ask whether X" here is asking the USER - they are the source of truth for X; never route to work to "verify" or "look up" what they can answer directly.

2. **Everything else is WORK - it acts on the world, or it composes and SENDS content through a channel to a recipient.** Research, browsing a website, fetching from a tool/file/API, querying the KG, calendar/todo/device/scheduler changes, running a tool, any multi-step work - AND composing and sending an email/text/message to a recipient ("email a family member the summary", "text the vendor", and even "email ME the report" - the deliverable is the composed email, not a UI ping).
   -> `run_work_node`. The worker (work_emi_team) carries it out and picks the right sub-tools/managers itself.

A node can mention "then notify me / report back" at the end - that suffix does NOT make the whole node a notification. Do the work first -> `run_work_node`; it surfaces the result when done.

# Tool catalog

++ `create_dayflow_ticket` - a UI notification or question to the USER themselves (notify, remind, tell, ask, nudge). It does NOT send any email or message - it is a UI ping to {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} only.

++ `run_work_node` - ANY node that DOES work, OR composes and sends an email/text/message to a recipient. The worker does it and chooses the right sub-tools/managers itself.

# Common failures to avoid

**Telling the USER to do something THEMSELVES is a TICKET, not work.** "Ask {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} to submit his timesheets", "Remind {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} to walk the dogs", "Nudge {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} to put down the screen", "Prompt {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} to resume sleep setup" -> `create_dayflow_ticket`. The worker cannot log in, walk the dogs, or sleep FOR the user - so it is a UI ping asking {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} to act, NOT a message you compose and send. {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} is the user, never an external recipient.

**Composing and SENDING content through a channel IS work.** "Email a family member the recommendation", "Email me the results", "text the vendor", "reply to the school" -> `run_work_node` (the worker composes + sends the actual email/text). The test: is content being composed and dispatched through a channel (work), or is a heads-up/question being surfaced in the user's UI (ticket)?

**"Notify + ask" the user is communicative.** "Notify {{ resource_user_data.first_name }} the dog-walk window opened and ask whether a family member already handled it" -> `create_dayflow_ticket`. The "ask" is to the user - they know whether it was handled; do NOT route to work to "verify" it.

**"Research + report" is WORK.** "Research X and submit / order / recommend / email it" -> `run_work_node`, not a ticket - bouncing a "do you want me to research?" question back to the user is exactly what they already approved.

